Package: robotcompR
Title: Robotics, Kinematics, Dynamics, and Motion Planning in R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Adam R", "Sophie", email = "adamrsophie@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: A scientific robotics computing framework for R. It provides
    validated spatial mathematics on SO(2), SO(3), SE(2) and SE(3)
    (rotation matrices, Euler angles, axis-angle, rotation vectors and
    scalar-first unit quaternions, exponential and logarithm maps with
    series expansions near the identity and robust handling near pi,
    adjoints and SO(3) Jacobians), rigid-body tree robot models with
    revolute, continuous, prismatic and fixed joints, standard and
    modified Denavit-Hartenberg models, 'URDF' import and export, forward
    kinematics, geometric and analytic Jacobians, manipulability and
    singularity analysis, numerical inverse kinematics (pseudoinverse,
    damped least squares and Levenberg-Marquardt with joint limits and
    restarts), rigid-body dynamics with the recursive Newton-Euler,
    composite rigid body and articulated body algorithms, torque-driven
    simulation, collision geometry with a GJK distance solver, sampling
    based motion planning (RRT, RRT-Connect, RRT* and PRM) with path
    shortcutting, polynomial and trapezoidal trajectories, unicycle,
    differential-drive and bicycle mobile robots, extended Kalman and
    particle filter localization, occupancy grid mapping and SE(2) pose
    graph optimization. The design is informed by the 'Robotics Toolbox
    for Python' <https://github.com/petercorke/robotics-toolbox-python>,
    'Pinocchio' <https://github.com/stack-of-tasks/pinocchio> and 'OMPL'
    <https://ompl.kavrakilab.org>; no 'MATLAB', 'Python', 'Julia' or
    'ROS 2' is required. The package is intended for research and
    education and is not certified for controlling physical hardware.
